The first clean run after the round 2 fixes (commit f5f2832) failed one step: large-5gib.
Cause: the reservation before every request (R2-02 fix) read the volume's 'available for important usage'
capacity with the coordinator's lock held; that query took about 20 ms idle on this host and longer while the
5 GiB check kept the disk busy, so jobViews() waited 425 ms (the R2-04 assertion, < 250 ms, caught it).
Fix: commit 712f8c0 reads free space before taking the lock (availableSpace()). Repeat runs after the fix:
review/round2-5gib-repeat.log. The clean run in ci-clean-run.log is the one after the fix.

